				<div class="leftcol game_description_column"  data-panel="{&quot;flow-children&quot;:&quot;column&quot;}" >

					
												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Coming Soon To Early Access</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">The developers of this game intend to release as a work in progress, developing with the feedback of players.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Tycoon games thrive when the community helps shape them. Our core loop (build<br />
your resort, manage it, react to events, and expand) is fully playable today,<br />
and Early Access lets us add depth, and features in the direction<br />
players actually want. We'd rather build the best ski resort sim with our<br />
players than guess in isolation.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“We're targeting roughly 12–18 months in Early Access, depending on community<br />
feedback.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Our goal for the full release is to build on the Early Access foundation while<br />
keeping the core loop intact. We're hoping to add more mountains around the world<br />
(Japan, the Alps, the Andes, Canada, Australia/New Zealand, China, the Himalayas,<br />
and more), along with additional building and lift content and visual upgrades.<br />
<br />
We also want to add new gameplay scenarios and new systems shaped together with<br />
the community, like terrain parks or summer activities, plus a broad balance<br />
pass.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Early Access is a full, playable resort sim. You can build trails, place lifts<br />
and more than 60 different buildings, and run a complete economy while thousands<br />
of simulated guests ski your mountain under a living snow-and-weather system. Five<br />
biomes are playable, each with multiple maps across a range of sizes,<br />
from small local hills to large destination resorts.<br />
<br />
Some art, audio, and UI are still being polished, and as an in-development game it<br />
will keep changing.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“Our current price reflects where the game is today. As we add new mountains, content, and features throughout Early Access, the price may increase to reflect that added value, so there's no downside to joining early.<br />
<br />
In the future, we'll consider adding paid DLC or additional content, as long as our community feels like we've shipped a complete game.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“Through a public roadmap, regular devlog updates, and an active Discord where<br />
players can report bugs, suggest features, and vote on priorities. Player<br />
feedback during Next Fest and Early Access will directly inform what we build<br />
next.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
